IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 2, s 8 -- who administers the Act, and what a person dealing with a Deputy
-- or Assistant Registrar may rely on. Layer 1 (the law, objectively): no seat is chosen here.
--
-- What is NOT encoded as a rule (inert, reason 2, machinery; the coverage table in NOTES.md says so row by row): s 8(1) (the Authority administers the Act),
-- s 8(1A) (the Minister appoints the Registrar and the Deputy and Assistant Registrars), s 8(1B) (the Authority directs the Registrar) and s 8(7) (the Minister
-- may amend five Schedules by notification). ss 8(5), (6) and (6A) are shown deleted.
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".

§ `Section 8(2): what a Deputy or Assistant Registrar may do`

-- src:2417 | (2) Subject to the general direction and control of the Registrar and
-- src:2418 | to such restrictions and limitations as may be prescribed, anything by
-- src:2419 | this Act appointed or authorised or required to be done or signed by
-- src:2420 | the Registrar may be done or signed by any such Deputy or Assistant
-- src:2421 | Registrar and is as valid and effectual as if done or signed by the
-- src:2422 | Registrar.
@ref s 8(2) (src:2417-2422)
GIVEN `the act is one that this Act appoints, authorises or requires the Registrar to do or sign` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was done or signed by a Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was done within the general direction and control of the Registrar and the restrictions and limitations that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) the act is as valid and effectual as if it had been done or signed by the Registrar` MEANS
    IF    `the act is one that this Act appoints, authorises or requires the Registrar to do or sign`
      AND `the act was done or signed by a Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar`
      AND `the act was done within the general direction and control of the Registrar and the restrictions and limitations that may be prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is "Subject to the general direction and control of the Registrar and to such restrictions and limitations as may be prescribed" and speaks only of acts the Act appoints, authorises or requires the Registrar to do or sign; it says nothing of an act outside those limits

§ `Section 8(3): the person dealing with a Deputy or Assistant Registrar`

-- src:2424 | (3) No person dealing with any Deputy or Assistant Registrar needs
-- src:2425 | to be concerned to see or inquire whether any restrictions or
-- src:2426 | limitations have been prescribed, and every act or omission of a
-- src:2427 | Deputy or Assistant Registrar so far as it affects any such person is as
-- src:2428 | valid and effectual as if done or omitted by the Registrar.
@ref s 8(3) (src:2424-2428)
GIVEN `the person is dealing with a Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the person dealing with a Deputy or Assistant Registrar needs to be concerned to see or inquire about prescribed restrictions or limitations` MEANS
    IF `the person is dealing with a Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person dealing with any Deputy or Assistant Registrar needs to be concerned to see or inquire whether any restrictions or limitations have been prescribed" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a person dealing with a Deputy or Assistant Registrar

-- src:2424 | (3) No person dealing with any Deputy or Assistant Registrar needs
-- src:2425 | to be concerned to see or inquire whether any restrictions or
-- src:2426 | limitations have been prescribed, and every act or omission of a
-- src:2427 | Deputy or Assistant Registrar so far as it affects any such person is as
-- src:2428 | valid and effectual as if done or omitted by the Registrar.
@ref s 8(3) (src:2424-2428)
GIVEN `the act or omission is an act or omission of a Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission affects the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the act or omission is as valid and effectual, so far as it affects the person, as if it had been done or omitted by the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission is an act or omission of a Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` AND `the act or omission affects the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every act or omission of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar so far as it affects any such person is as valid and effectual as if done or omitted by the Registrar" says nothing of an act that does not affect the person or of an act of anyone else

§ `Section 8(4): judicial notice of the Registrar's seal and signature`

-- src:2432 | (4) All courts, judges and persons acting judicially are to take
-- src:2433 | judicial notice of the seal and signature of the Registrar and of any
-- src:2434 | Deputy or Assistant Registrar.
@ref s 8(4) (src:2432-2434)
GIVEN `the seal or signature is the seal or signature of the Registrar or of a Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal is a court, a judge or a person acting judicially` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(4) the tribunal is to take judicial notice of the seal or signature` MEANS
    IF `the seal or signature is the seal or signature of the Registrar or of a Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` AND `the tribunal is a court, a judge or a person acting judicially`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names the seal and signature of the Registrar, Deputy and Assistant Registrars and the courts, judges and persons acting judicially; it says nothing of any other seal or tribunal
